  "changes": [
    {
      "change": "Restore the four ROM driver headers and installation loop.",
      "reason": "The patch adds a RAM signature before each header. The ROM instead installs the headers directly and uses the shared InClose entry at $41B9D8. Symbolic offsets reproduce every header byte."
    },
    {
      "change": "Restore local-memory storage, inline handle locking, and the original DTR setup.",
      "reason": "The ROM stores port variables at $2D0 and $2D8 and locks handles by setting bit 7. Later patches use expanded memory for port B and change DTR initialization. InitDefs in this ROM contains $8A as the final WR5 constant."
    },
    {
      "change": "Retain the original input-flow branch and fixed clock initialization.",
      "reason": "The BNE at $41BE46 targets CheckBufferFull at $41BE18. PatchPlusROM.a describes the later repair to target Put at $41BE4C. The ROM also lacks the later external-clock control path."
    },
    {
      "change": "Recover missing code as 68000 instructions with source field names.",
      "reason": "This tree lacks the original standalone serial driver source. The patch retains enough layout and code to identify the main routines; ROM instructions supply the remaining paths. New comments carry a Reconstruction marker. Matching historical comments remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "change": "Make assembler choices explicit.",
      "reason": "PC-relative operands, branch sizes, table boundaries, and trap OPWORD definitions specify the target encodings. The driver uses the $A53D form of DrvrInstall. The generated source contains instructions for code and declarations for data."
    }
  ],
